        "description": "What a hosted call does to a lease (S10, N11): a credential the provider issues for one resource a call creates, held by runx Connect for the resource's owner. Connect applies it at the provider's answer, so a leased value never reaches the kernel, which sees only the lease's evidence (its target, expiry and the value's digest). A lease is keyed by connector, credential and target, so a seller leases resources only in its own connector. Each action carries only what it needs: a take names the new resource, and a renew or a release acts on the operation's own target.",
